# GlassElt= is matched by its FULL name (2026-11-01, PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2; found by TO building the lens catalog).
# Before, LCMP over one name's length was a PREFIX match at all three lookup sites: MOD GlassElt(6)=SF10 took SF1's
# Sellmeier row (49 catalog names are captured by a shorter earlier row that way: SF10..SF19 by SF1, SF53..SF59 by
# SF5, BaSF10/12/13 by BaSF1, SK10..SK18A by SK1, FK51/52/54 by FK5, ...), and a deck naming a glass that is not in
# the table but is a prefix of a row (SF) took that row with no message.  Now MOD SF10 writes SF10's row, a deck's
# unknown name is SAID at load (warns, never refuses) and the element keeps its IndRef, and the two rows added the
# same day resolve by name (N-SF5, N-F2: the Schott datasheet-collection constants, the Newport achromats' glasses).
# Non-vacuity: must_fail/glasselt_prefix.jou asserts the old capture and must NOT pass.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in
cd $TMP
old ImageDemo.in
mod
GlassElt(6)=SF10
q
save sf10
mod
GlassElt(6)=N-SF5
q
save nsf5
mod
GlassElt(6)=N-F2
q
save nf2
! cp $DECK sf.in
! perl -i -pe 's/^(\s*IndRef=\s+1\.61783d\+00)$/$1\n  GlassElt=  SF/' sf.in
old sf.in
save sfsaid
! grep -A2 'GlassElt=' sf10.in nsf5.in nf2.in
! grep -c 'GlassElt=' sfsaid.in
! grep 'IndRef=' sfsaid.in
# EXPECT: GlassElt\(\s*6\) = SF10
# EXPECT: sf10\.in-\s*GlassCoef=\s+1\.616259
# EXPECT: nsf5\.in-\s*GlassCoef=\s+1\.524818
# EXPECT: nf2\.in-\s*GlassCoef=\s+1\.397570
# EXPECT: sf\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?\*\* GlassElt= SF \(elt\s+6\): not in the glass table
# An unresolved name is not SAVEd: the element keeps its IndRef (SAVE writes GlassElt only for a resolved glass).
# EXPECT: grep -c 'GlassElt=' sfsaid\.in\s+0\s
# EXPECT: grep 'IndRef=' sfsaid\.in[\s\S]*?IndRef=\s*1\.61783
# EXPECT-NOT: Replace\? \[YES\]
# EXPECT-NOT: GlassCoef=\s+1\.55912923
# EXPECT-NOT: Unknown glass
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
